      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dafter_Township%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Dafter sits about a mile southwest of the junction of M‑28 and I‑75, within the Waiska River drainage basin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dafter_Township%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The township is part of Chippewa County, one of Michigan’s Upper Peninsula counties known for its rugged shoreline.",
